title: radio_02_hunger
freq: 38.75
left: vulture
right: deer,sterna,bear
name: Call 02 — Hunger
---
vulture: Vulture here. I heard gunfire.¶Report.
<<if not $dead_sterna>>
    sterna: Putain.¶Contact. One crew member, out of a berth on B Deck.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    bear: Contact, boss. One crew member.¶Came out of a berth on B Deck.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    deer: Contact, sir. One crew member.¶Came out of a berth on B Deck.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear>>
    bear: He saw us and came straight at us. No weapon, no warning.¶He wasn't trying to fight, boss. He was trying to bite.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    sterna: He saw us and came straight at us. No weapon, niente.¶He wasn't fighting, Vulture. He was trying to bite.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    deer: He came straight at us, sir. No weapon.¶He wasn't fighting. He was biting.
<<endif>>
_beat: silence
<<if not $dead_sterna>>
    <<if $dead_deer>>
        sterna: Allora.¶The kid was right. That wasn't rage, Vulture. That was hunger.
    <<else>>
        sterna: Allora.¶What Bambi told us was true. That wasn't rage, Vulture. That was hunger.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    <<if $dead_deer and $dead_sterna>>
        bear: The kid was right.¶That wasn't rage, boss. That was hunger.
    <<else>>
        bear: What the kid told us was true.¶That wasn't rage, boss. That was hunger.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    deer: It's the same thing I saw, sir.¶They're starving.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear>>
    bear: Boss. If the rest of the crew is like that one...¶how many are we talking about?
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    sterna: Vulture. If the rest of the crew is like that one...¶quanti? How many are we talking about?
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    deer: Sir. If the rest of the crew is like that one...¶how many?
<<endif>>
vulture: A hull that size runs twenty to thirty hands.
vulture: Assume all of them.
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_deer>>
    deer: Sir.¶That's twenty to thirty people still aboard.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_deer>>
    deer: Are we still treating them as survivors?
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer>>
    vulture: I'm treating them as hostile.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and not $dead_deer>>
    sterna: Genau.¶Whatever that was, it stopped being crew a long time ago.
<<endif>>
_beat: silence
vulture: Casualties?
<<if not $dead_bear and not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and not $dead_bear>>
    bear: None.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and $dead_deer>>
    <<if $dead_deer and $dead_sterna>>
        bear: The kid didn't make it, boss.¶Sterna's gone too.
    <<else>>
        bear: The kid didn't make it, boss.
    <<endif>>
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and $dead_deer and $dead_bear>>
    sterna: The kid didn't make it.¶Bear's gone too. Los dos.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and $dead_deer>>
    sterna: Merde.¶He walked out of that first boarding alive, and he didn't last the night.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and $dead_deer>>
    bear: He told us he wouldn't be dead weight.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and not $dead_bear and $dead_deer and $dead_sterna>>
    bear: Sterna went down covering him.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and not $dead_sterna and $dead_deer and $dead_bear>>
    sterna: Bear went down first.¶He was trying to reach the kid. Il a essayé.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and not $dead_bear and $dead_deer>>
    vulture: That's a loss.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and not $dead_bear and $dead_deer>>
    vulture: Stay focused. We still have a ship to clear.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and not $dead_bear and $dead_deer>>
    _beat: silence
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and $dead_deer and $dead_sterna>>
    vulture: Sterna.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and $dead_deer and $dead_sterna>>
    _beat: silence
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and $dead_deer and $dead_bear>>
    vulture: Bear.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and $dead_deer and $dead_bear>>
    _beat: silence
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and not $dead_deer and not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    bear: We lost Sterna.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    vulture: One man. Unarmed.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    vulture: I trained her for eleven years and she goes down to one unarmed man.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    vulture: You were both busy keeping the kid breathing instead of watching your own backs.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_deer and not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    deer: ...Understood, sir.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and not $dead_deer and not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    bear: That's enough, boss.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and not $dead_deer and not $dead_bear and $dead_sterna>>
    bear: From here on he stays with me.¶If something gets to him, it goes through me first.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    sterna: We lost Bear.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    vulture: One man. Unarmed.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    vulture: Bear has opened his way into forty ships and he goes down to one unarmed man.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    vulture: You were both busy keeping the kid breathing instead of watching your own backs.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    deer: ...Understood, sir.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    _beat: silence
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    sterna: Bambi.¶Écoute-moi.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    sterna: Stay close to me and keep your head up.¶Life gets very short out here. En un segundo, y ya está.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_deer and $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    deer: I'm alone, sir.¶Sterna and Bear are both gone.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    _beat: silence
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    vulture: Both of them.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    vulture: I came aboard with three of my people, Coast Guard.¶Now I have you.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_deer and $dead_sterna and $dead_bear>>
    deer: ...Understood, sir.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_bear and $dead_deer and $dead_sterna>>
    vulture: You're the only one left out there, Bear.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_sterna and $dead_deer and $dead_bear>>
    vulture: You're the only one left out there, Sterna.
<<endif>>
<<if not $dead_deer and not $dead_sterna and not $dead_bear>>
    vulture: Listen to me, all three of you.
<<else>>
    vulture: Listen to me.
<<endif>>
vulture: Long range is still jammed. I cannot reach Command.
vulture: If one of you takes a serious hit out there, I have no way to get you off this ship.
vulture: No evac. No medevac. Nothing.
_beat: silence
vulture: So don't take one.
vulture: Keep the channel open.¶Vulture out.
===
